                   Documentation for Neutron-LastCallers
                  ---------------------------------------

Introduction:

                This is a powerful Last-10-Callers (Door?) for
                AmiExpress (/X) 4.x. It is faast, nice looking
                and can handle a lot of errors that could ocur
                during a user connect time. (carrier loss, sys
                tem crash, and so on...)In the registered vers
                ion you will be able to create your own design
                for this great door. In this version are two d
                esigns included: Number one is designed by my-
                self and the second one was taken from Amfetam
                in / © The Silencer.

Requirements:   
                Any Amiga Computer with installed/working /X.

Features:       
                Shows:  Handle
                        Location
                        Logindate
                        Logintime
                        Logofftime
                        Download
                        failed Download
                        Upload
                        failes Upload
                        new User
                        Bulletins Viewer (if supported)
                        operator Paged (if supported)
                        Operator Chat
                        examine Restricted Files
                        file scan
                        conference scan
                        pw failures / hack tries
                        account edit
                        carrier lost

Installation:   
                Just copy the drawer to your doors directory.
                Add the following line to every logoffbatch
                in your bbs:commands/syscmd drawer:

                doors:ntr-lastcallers/ntr-lastcallers x

                the x stands for each node number (off course)
                the bulletin will be created as:

                bbs:bulletins/lastc.txt

                you have just to view it in /X with something like:

                ~
                ~SS_BBS:BULLETINS/LASTC.txt

                Now you have to create the datafiles.

                1) Open a cli window.
                2) type "doors:ntr-lastcallers/ntr-lastcallers 0"
                   (you have just created the datas for node 0)
                3) repeat step 2 for each node you have, remember
                   to replace the 0 with the nodenumber!

Configuration:  
                There is a CONFIG file in the drawer.

                First Line / Sysop:

                        Put here a "1" to show the sysop in the bull
                     or put here a "0" to hide the sysop in the bull.

                Secon Line / Design:

                        1 : Gravedancers Design,     No ANSI-Header
                        2 : Design from Amfetamin,   No ANSI-Header
                        3 : Gravedancers Design,   With ANSI-Header
                        4 : Design from Amfetamin, With ANSI-Header
                        5 : Use your own design (registered Version only)

                        The Ansi-Header is © by Tango/aC!

                Example configuration is set to:

                No Sysop in the bulletin
                Gravedancer Design with Header

Making your own design:

First you have to create a file called "DESIGN.1". It includes the information
you want to be shown in the bull. The followin keywords can be used:

                             ND ... NODENUMBER
                     =====HANDLE===== ... THE USERNAME
                    ====!LOCATION!==== ... THE LOCATION
                           BAUD ... CONNECT BAUD
                            ==D== ... LOGONDATE
                            XX:XX ... LOGONTIME
                           YY:YY ... LOGOFFTIME
                         ?U ... NUMBER OF UPLOADS
                        ?D ... NUMBER OF DOWNLOADS
                           =U!= ... UPLOADBYTES
                          =D!= ... DOWNLOADBYTES
                    STATS ... STATUSLINE #1 (SEE BELOW)
                  STATS-TWO ... STATUSLINE #2 (SEE BELOW)
                 % ... USERSTATUS (WHETHER NEWUSER OR NOT)

STATUSLINE #1 INCLUDES INFORMATION ABOUT:
                                          CARRIER LOST
                                          NEWUSER
                                          HACKEDPW
                                          SYSOP PAGE
                                          FILESCAN

STATUSLINE #1 INCLUDES INFORMATION ABOUT: 
                                          PWFAIL
                                          UPLOAD
                                          DOWNLOAD
                                          SYSOP PAGE
                                          FILESCAN
                                          BULLETINS
                                          CARRIER LOST
                                          ACCOUNT EDITOR
                                          RESTRICTED FILES

EXAMPLE:

[36mND [0m=====HANDLE===== ====!LOCATION!====  [33mXX:XX[35m-[33mYY:YY STATS ?U:=U!= ?D:=D!= [36mBAUD[0m

(this looks like the included Amfetamin design, doesn't it?)

Second step is to design the complete layout, called DESIGN.2.

EXAMPLE: (again looking like the amfetamin design ...)

 [0;1;35m ___[36m.[35m_ _______________________________________[36m.[35m_ _____[36m.[35m_ ___________________
 [0;1;35m(  ¬[36m|[35m___[36m.[35m____  /  ____   [36m_[35m¬\   [36m.[35m___[36m.[35m____  /  ¬[36ml[35m___[36m.[35m  ¬[36ml[35m__[36m.[35m  _______  _/  ___)
 [0;1;35m/   [36m|[35m  ¬[36m|[35m   [36m_[35m  \___ ¬\   [36m|[35m_/   [36m|[35m  ¬[36m|[35m   [36m_[35m  \   [36m|[35m  ¬[36m|[35m   [36m|[35m ¬[36m|[35m  ___)  [36m_[35m   \___ ¬\
 [0;1;35m\____   [36ml[35m___[36m|[35m  ______/___[36m|[35m \____   [36m|[35m   [36m|[35m__/____   [36ml[35m____  [36ml[35m________[36m|[35m   ______/
 [0;1;35m    `---[36m'[35m   [36m`[35m---'              `---[36m'[35m---'[36mtGø[35m   `---[36m'[35m   `--[36m'[35m       ¬[36m`[35m----'

[36mNd User Name        Location            TimeOnBoard ACTVT U#/Byte D#/Byte Rate
[34m-- ---------------- ------------------- ----------- ----- ------- ------- ----
=LASTCALLERS=
[34;1m-------------------------------------------------------------------------------[0m
[33m([36mC[33m)[32marrier Lost, [33m([36mN[33m)[32mew User, [33m([36mH[33m)[32macked Passwords, [33m([36mP[33m)[32maged SysOp, [33m([36mS[33m)[32mcanned Files
[34;1m-------------------------------------------------------------------------------[0m
=TODAYSTATS=
=YESTERDAYSTATS=
=RECORDS=
[34;1m-------------------------------------------------------------------------------[0m

AGAIN YOU CAN USE SPECIAL KEYWORDS:

       =LASTCALLERS= ... STARTING POSITION FOR THE LASTCALLERS LINES
        =TODAYSTATS= ... TODAY STATISTICS (AS IN AMFETAMIN DESIGN)
    =YESTERDAYSTATS= ... YESTERDAY STATISTICS (AS IN AMFETAMIN DESIGN)
         =RECORDS= ... RECORD STATISTICS (AS IN AMFETAMIN DESIGN)

The Future:
                There will be soon a online-tool that views the bulletin
                and that highlights the current user - if he is in the
                bulletin.

                Example:
                         User Gravedancer called the bbs and left it.
                         He calls back and the bull is shown to him !
                         The last caller was he (which wonder!) and
                         the line which includes the data of his call
                         is highlighted !!! (special-nonsense-feature)

